&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animation (in Italian) showing motion of α Centauri through the sky. (The other stars are held fixed for didactic reasons.) \"Oggi\" means today; \"anni\" means years.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlpha_Cen_proper_motions.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Orbital_plot_of_Proxima_Centauri.jpg/500px-Orbital_plot_of_Proxima_Centauri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Orbital_plot_of_Proxima_Centauri.jpg/500px-Orbital_plot_of_Proxima_Centauri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orbital plot of Proxima Centauri around the bright apparent star Alpha Centauri AB, with position change marked (in thousands of years).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrbital_plot_of_Proxima_Centauri.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Orbit_Alpha_Centauri_AB_arcsec.png/500px-Orbit_Alpha_Centauri_AB_arcsec.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Orbit_Alpha_Centauri_AB_arcsec.png/500px-Orbit_Alpha_Centauri_AB_arcsec.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apparent and true orbits of Alpha Centauri. The A component is held stationary, and the relative orbital motion of the B component is shown. The apparent orbit (thin ellipse) is the shape of the orbit as seen by an observer on Earth. The true orbit is the shape of the orbit viewed perpendicular to the plane of the orbital motion. According to the radial velocity versus time,[102] the radial separation of A and B along the line of sight had reached a maximum in 2007, with B being further from Earth than A. The orbit is divided here into 80 points: each step refers to a timestep of approx. 0.99888 years or 364.84 days.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrbit_Alpha_Centauri_AB_arcsec.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ESO_-_Alpha_Centauri_in_the_HR-System_%28by%29.jpg/500px-ESO_-_Alpha_Centauri_in_the_HR-System_%28by%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ESO_-_Alpha_Centauri_in_the_HR-System_%28by%29.jpg/500px-ESO_-_Alpha_Centauri_in_the_HR-System_%28by%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ESO - Alpha Centauri in the HR-System (by)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AESO_-_Alpha_Centauri_in_the_HR-System_(by).jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey squirrel (Sciurus carolinensis) 02","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Grey_squirrel_%28Sciurus_carolinensis%29_02.jpg/500px-Grey_squirrel_%28Sciurus_carolinensis%29_02.jpg","ratio":1.4993498049414824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_squirrel_(Sciurus_carolinensis)_02.jpg","share":0.0925},{"title":"Grey 2019 by Glenn Francis","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Grey_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg/500px-Grey_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg","ratio":0.6666006731340328,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg","share":0.090625},{"title":"Toliman in Khimki Reservoir 2016-05-12 Pic 04","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Toliman_in_Khimki_Reservoir_2016-05-12_Pic_04.JPG/500px-Toliman_in_Khimki_Reservoir_2016-05-12_Pic_04.JPG","ratio":1.4998560322487762,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toliman_in_Khimki_Reservoir_2016-05-12_Pic_04.JPG","share":0.08625},{"title":"The predicted trajectory of Alpha Centauri A and B (ann16075a)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/The_predicted_trajectory_of_Alpha_Centauri_A_and_B_%28ann16075a%